{"purpose":"Enable eka-cli to install and manage plugins — the official eka-mcp plugin and third-party plugins — with an explicit trust model, so the MCP integration is distributed without manual copying and without violating the eka-cli -\u003e eka-mcp dependency prohibition.","content":"- eka-cli SHALL provide `eka plugin install \u003cname\u003e` to install the official mcp plugin by name from a hardcoded registry. - eka-cli SHALL verify the SHA-256 checksum of every downloaded plugin binary (fail-closed). - eka-cli SHALL provide `eka plugin list`, `remove`, and `update` for plugin lifecycle. - eka-cli SHALL treat registry-listed (maleolabs) plugins as full-trust (no consent prompt) and all others as third-party (explicit consent + capability review). - The plugin manifest SHALL declare `capabilities` (v1: install + mcp) and `source`. - eka-mcp SHALL publish release binaries `eka-mcp-\u003cos\u003e-\u003carch\u003e[.exe]` plus SHA256SUMS.txt."}